From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 02:36:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: run chunk decoration off the server thread

Splits populate into three stages - structures/lakes/dungeons, decoration,
then the animals and the snow - and puts the middle one on a single decoration
thread for the whole server, with its world calls redirected into a sandbox
that buffers the blocks it chooses. The server thread replays them through the
real setTypeAndData, so lighting, client updates and physics still happen where
they always did.

With the feature off the generated world is bit-identical to master (0 of 625
chunks differ), so the refactor itself is neutral. With it on it is not, for
two reasons that the measurement pinned down and that are recorded in the next
commit message rather than fixed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

